  ],
  "decision": "Top-level keys in order: root, files, languages, totals. files = list sorted by relative path (same order as text table), each {path, language, lines}. languages = object keyed by language value, sorted by name, each {files, lines}. totals = {files, lines}. Paths emitted with forward slashes (as_posix).",
  "risks": [
    "text and JSON path separators differ on Windows; a test normalises before comparing"
  ],
  "why": "Mirrors the text output's data (path/language/lines columns, sorted rows, language list, file count) so totals can be compared 1:1. Sorted keys and files make output deterministic for diffing. Short names are enough; lines matches the text column header. Forward slashes make JSON identical across OSes while text keeps native separators for byte-for-byte compatibility."
